\subsection{Cross-Suite Generalization}
\label{sec:cross_suite}

The cliff zone exhibits a suite $\times$ method interaction: at $k \leq 0.7$, pruning behavior is task-independent; at $k \in [0.85, 0.95]$, Object tasks collapse under random removal while Spatial tasks degrade gracefully (Table~\ref{tab:pi05_crosssuite}, Appendix~\ref{app:pi05_crosssuite}). L2 norm maintains a near-baseline plateau in random's cliff zone on both suites ($\leq 2.4$\,pp at $k \geq 0.85$; no sudden $>$20\,pp collapse). CV$\,{=}\,$0.055 correctly predicts this plateau on both Object (precision-critical) and Spatial (layout-critical) suites, despite qualitatively different random cliff profiles---confirming CV as a model-level diagnostic rather than a task-specific one.
